Objective
	Goals: G1, G2, G3, ..., Gn
	Minimize MAX(T(G1), T(G2), T(G3), ..., T(Gn))
	Do not optimize the completion time of a goal in isolation
	Prioritize actions that reduce the projected completion time of all goals

Critical Path
	Estimate which goals currently determine or threaten the projected completion time
	Prioritize goals on the critical path
	Prioritize goals near the critical path over goals with large slack
	Do not prioritize a local deadline unless missing it can increase the projected completion time
	Re-evaluate the critical path when the state changes significantly

Eligibility
	An action is eligible only if
		It is still pending
		Its dependencies are satisfied
		Its temporal and environmental conditions are satisfied
		Its required resources are available
		Using its resources does not interfere with a higher-priority action
	If an unexpected state or unhandled condition is observed
		Stop execution
		Return to Planner

Daily Execution
	At start of day
		Evaluate all eligible actions

	☣️ Critical Execution
		Execute all eligible ☣️ actions before accepting the timeline
		If an action causes the day to restart
			Restart ☣️ Critical Execution
		Continue until all eligible ☣️ actions are resolved
		Accept timeline

	Production Maintenance
		Maintain infrastructure that contributes to the current critical path
		Prevent productive bottleneck infrastructure from remaining idle
		Do not prioritize maintenance of infrastructure with sufficient slack over critical-path production

	Production Expansion
		Identify the current production bottleneck
		Expand the bottleneck
		Do not expand non-bottleneck infrastructure unless needed for an upcoming bottleneck
		Re-evaluate the bottleneck after significant expansion

	Goal Progression
		Progress eligible goals according to their threat to the projected completion time
		Prioritize critical-path goals
		Then prioritize near-critical goals
		Defer goals with sufficient slack

	Free Time
		If no eligible action can reduce the projected completion time
			Do whatever

Day Utilization
	If an eligible productive action can still reduce the projected completion time
		Do not sleep early
		Continue working until 2:00am
		Do not return to Farmhouse only to avoid passing out
		Passing out at 2:00am is acceptable when the remaining cost is negligible compared with the value of the extra productive time
		Do not intentionally allow Health to reach 0
	Else
		Sleeping early is allowed
